<%#
  What the last row or column action did, and a way back (WP6).

  A row or column action changes the screen and nothing else -- only Save
  writes -- and before this there was nothing on the page saying either of
  those things. One click could change a hundred cells with no count, no way
  back short of reloading, and no hint that reloading was the way back.

  Empty and hidden until an action runs; the script fills it in and shows it.
  aria-live so the count is announced rather than only drawn, and the undo is a
  plain link -- one tab stop, with the browser's own focus ring, which Redmine's
  stylesheet removes on form controls but never on an <a>, on any supported
  version.

  tabindex="-1" is what lets the script move focus *here* before it hides the
  undo link. Undoing until the stack empties otherwise leaves focus on the
  element that is then hidden, and it falls back to <body> -- the next Tab
  restarts at the top of the page, past the sentence that has just changed
  (finding F15). -1 rather than 0: this is a focus target the script hands over
  to, never a tab stop of its own.

  Rendered above the matrix from the two partials that are already there: the
  administration screens' note, and a project matrix's header. Not from an
  anchor of its own, because it needs none, and not from the script's own <td>,
  which is inside the table it talks about.

  The strings come down as data attributes rather than being built in the
  script, so every sentence on the page stays in the locale files. The names
  match the confirmation's convention: %{...} placeholders, replaced in the
  browser.
%>
<div id="project-workflow-bulk-undo" class="project-workflow-bulk-undo" style="display:none;"
     aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"
     data-project-workflow-changed="<%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_changed) %>"
     data-project-workflow-undone="<%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_undone) %>">
  <span class="project-workflow-bulk-undo-message"></span>
  <%= link_to_function l(:button_project_workflow_bulk_undo), 'projectWorkflowBulkUndo()',
                       class: 'project-workflow-bulk-undo-action',
                       'aria-label' => l(:button_project_workflow_bulk_undo) %>
  <em><%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_unsaved) %></em>
</div>
